  "text": "Here's the solution:\n\n```python\nimport re\n\ndef word_histogram(text):\n    # Convert text to lowercase and remove punctuation using regular expression\n    cleaned_text = re.sub(r'[^\\w\\s]', '', text.lower())\n    \n    # Split the text into words\n    words = cleaned_text.split()\n    \n    # Create a histogram dictionary\n    histogram = {}\n    for word in words:\n        if word in histogram:\n            histogram[word] += 1\n        else:\n            histogram[word] = 1\n    \n    return histogram\n```\n\nThis code:\n1. Converts the input text to lowercase\n2. Removes any punctuation using regular expression\n3. Splits the text into individual words\n4. Counts the frequency of each word in the dictionary\n\nThe implementation meets all the requirements specified in the unit tests, including the expected behavior for the given test cases.",
